1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,735
A test screening tells you the audience
got bored. It does not tell you where.

2
00:00:04,735 --> 00:00:07,709
MomentLab answers that question with a
timestamp.

3
00:00:09,709 --> 00:00:13,192
35,001 respondents watched this scene.

4
00:00:13,192 --> 00:00:20,434
Across roughly 2 million playback events,
retention drops 18.1% at 37 seconds —

5
00:00:20,434 --> 00:00:23,734
inside a window from 00:33 to 00:41.

6
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:31,175
Retention is aggregated per age cohort in
ClickHouse, in an AggregatingMergeTree

7
00:00:31,175 --> 00:00:36,480
materialized view. The curve you're seeing
came back in about 45 milliseconds.

8
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:41,105
The same question against raw events takes
roughly three times that.

9
00:00:43,105 --> 00:00:48,199
This is a Google ADK agent running Gemini
2.5 Pro on Vertex AI.

10
00:00:48,199 --> 00:00:54,749
When I re-run the analysis, it queries
ClickHouse through the official ClickHouse

11
00:00:54,749 --> 00:00:59,034
MCP server and forms a hypothesis from
what it finds.

12
00:01:01,034 --> 00:01:03,131
The indicator is not decorative.

13
00:01:03,131 --> 00:01:08,633
It reflects real service health and the
number of agent runs in the last 15

14
00:01:08,633 --> 00:01:10,926
When nothing has run, it says idle.

15
00:01:12,926 --> 00:01:15,732
Every query the agent ran is recorded —

16
00:01:15,732 --> 00:01:19,330
up to 50 executions, with duration and row
counts.

17
00:01:19,330 --> 00:01:23,143
This is the agent's actual work, not a
summary of it.

18
00:01:25,143 --> 00:01:32,666
Open any one of them and you get the query
ID, the execution time, the rows read,

19
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:36,753
and the exact SQL. 3 milliseconds, 737
rows.

20
00:01:36,753 --> 00:01:41,304
You can verify the number instead of
trusting it.

21
00:01:43,304 --> 00:01:49,648
Every figure carries its state. PREDICTED
means a forecast. MEASURED means a result.

22
00:01:49,648 --> 00:01:53,198
GROUNDED means real ClickHouse queries
back it.

23
00:01:53,198 --> 00:01:58,258
Nothing is called verified unless the
system actually confirmed it.

24
00:02:00,258 --> 00:02:03,029
The agent proposes. A person approves.

25
00:02:03,029 --> 00:02:08,717
This edit is a testable proposal with a
predicted effect and a reviewer gate —

26
00:02:08,717 --> 00:02:10,103
not an instruction.

27
00:02:12,103 --> 00:02:20,393
The cut measured an 11.1% engagement lift,
95% confidence interval from +10.9% to

28
00:02:20,393 --> 00:02:28,171
+11.4%, across 17,500 respondents per arm.
Only then is it labeled MEASURED.

29
00:02:30,171 --> 00:02:32,682
No cameras. No facial recognition.

30
00:02:32,682 --> 00:02:38,739
Only consented in-player reactions,
aggregated behind a minimum cohort size of

31
00:02:38,739 --> 00:02:41,324
The demo runs on a seeded dataset —

32
00:02:41,324 --> 00:02:45,534
the agent, the queries and the measurement
path are real.

33
00:02:45,534 --> 00:02:50,187
MomentLab turns “it dragged” into a frame
range you can act on.
